            // 8-byte stride so an f64 field fits — header 8 + nf*8 bytes, field i
            // at 8+i*8 (matching the register backends). An 8-byte INTEGER field
            // (i64/u64) stores via i64.store; an 8-byte FLOAT field (f64/f32/float —
            // f32 is f64-backed) via f64.store through the f64 scratch; others via
            // i32.store. The width classification mirrors struct_set / struct_get
